    "deck_permits_engineering_4C48gw": {
      "type": "deck-permits-engineering",
      "name": "Deck Permits/Engineering",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "New York Deck Permits and A-DIY Engineering Information",
        "body_text": "<p>A permit may be required depending on the deck's dimensions, height, location, attachment method and local rules.</p><p>The New York State Uniform Code establishes minimum construction standards throughout the state except New York City. Local cities, towns, villages and counties generally administer and enforce the applicable codes. New York City maintains its own construction-code and permit system.</p><p>Requirements may differ between neighboring municipalities.</p>",
        "questions_heading": "Questions to Ask the Building Department",
        "questions_list": "Does the proposed deck require a permit?\nIs zoning approval, a site plan or a survey required?\nWhat setbacks apply?\nAre stamped plans required?\nWhat footing information must be submitted?\nWhat inspections are required?\nAre stairs or railings required at the proposed height?\nCan the homeowner perform the work?",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Frame_2147260189.png",
        "note_title": "New York City",
        "note_text": "New York City homeowners must follow current Department of Buildings requirements. The city may require approved plans and design work completed by a New York State licensed professional engineer or registered architect.",
        "section_bg": "#ffffff",
        "accent_border_color": "#c67d3e",
        "padding_top_desktop": 64,
        "padding_bottom_desktop": 64,
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40
      }
    },
    "engineering_diagrams_zHUnjj": {
      "type": "engineering-diagrams",
      "name": "Engineering Diagrams",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "What Do A-DIY Engineering Diagrams Show?",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Product-img-removebg-preview_1_6cddae38-6e96-4116-b94b-d6c29b439bde.png",
        "list_heading": "Diagrams for an applicable A-DIY configuration may show:",
        "list_items": "Overall dimensions and structural layout\nBeam and joist locations\nPost locations\nLumber dimensions\nMajor connections\nAssembly configuration",
        "body_text": "<p>The building department may still request property-specific information, such as a survey, site plan, setbacks, foundation details, stairs, railings, attachment details or professionally stamped documents.</p><p>Requirements vary by municipality, and the local building department has final authority. A-DIY diagrams can support a permit application but do not guarantee approval.</p>",
        "section_bg": "#f5f5f3",
        "padding_top_desktop": 64,
        "padding_bottom_desktop": 64,
        "padding_top_mobile": 40,
        "padding_bottom_mobile": 40
      }
